{"chunk_id": "969ceae5a4dc", "text": "After the demon Trishiras wounds Rama, the prince responds with overwhelming precision: he destroys the demon\u2019s chariot, slays his horses and charioteer, and finally severs his three heads. The surviving rakshasas flee, but their leader Khara\u2014enraged by the destruction of his army and generals\u2014charges into battle. What follows is a vast, storm-like duel. Rama and Khara fill the sky with arrows until the sun itself seems darkened. Khara briefly gains advantage by shattering Rama\u2019s bow and armor, but Rama calmly takes up the divine Vaishnava bow given by the sage Agastya. With dazzling archery he destroys Khara\u2019s banner, chariot, horses, and weapons. As the demon stands on foot with a mace, the gods and sages gather in the sky to witness the heroic confrontation, recognizing Rama\u2019s extraordinary might and righteousness.\nRama defeats Trishiras and then engages Khara in a fierce duel, destroying his chariot and overpowering him while the gods watch in awe.\nThemes: heroic combat, divine justice, dharma vs tyranny, warrior honor, cosmic spectatorship", "vector": [-0.00030423933640122414, -0.014152389019727707, -0.0040935552679002285, 0.0023346056696027517, -0.014408236369490623, 0.011062025092542171, -0.03239833563566208, -0.03659961372613907, -0.02468252182006836, -0.018771104514598846, 0.016104906797409058, 0.017464937642216682, -0.004362867679446936, 0.010920635424554348, 0.006914606783539057, 0.022097118198871613, 0.03288309648633003, -0.027537237852811813, 0.0265811774879694, -0.014098526909947395, 0.006035973783582449, -0.006689057685434818, -0.003150960197672248, 0.024157362058758736, -0.033448655158281326, 0.015162312425673008, 0.024897972121834755, -0.024601727724075317, 0.007264713756740093, -0.026365727186203003, -0.0013221576809883118, -0.01446209941059351, -0.0022066819947212934, -0.006880942732095718, -0.016737792640924454, 0.008759399875998497, 0.010536864399909973, -0.000988041516393423,